---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title='About · Benji Tusk' description='About Benji Tusk and this engineering notebook.' width='prose'>
    <Hero title='About' compact>
        <Eyebrow slot='eyebrow' tone='accent'>Who's writing this</Eyebrow>
        <Fragment slot='lede'>
            I'm Benji, a software engineer in Jerusalem who likes taking things apart to see how they work.
        </Fragment>
    </Hero>

    <Prose>
        <p>
            Most of my time goes into <a href='https://schedulearn.com' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'
                >ScheduLearn</a
            >, a scheduling tool for schools that I cofounded while I was still in university. I take care of the
            backend and the cloud infrastructure it runs on, and the day-to-day frontend work too. I finished my BSc in
            Mathematics and Computer Science at the Jerusalem College of Technology in 2026.
        </p>
        <p>
            Outside of that, my projects have mostly been things I didn't know how to build when I started. For a long
            time that meant software: browser games, WhatsApp and Reddit bots, an iOS Reddit client, and an app for the
            yeshiva I studied at. A few of them ended up being used by real people. A lot of them never got finished,
            which is fine, since that's usually where I learned the most.
        </p>
        <p>
            More recently I've started getting into reverse engineering: figuring out how undocumented hardware,
            protocols, and firmware work, and getting them to do things they weren't built to do. Those projects come
            with even less certainty about how they'll turn out, which makes them a good fit for this notebook.
        </p>

        <h2>What this is</h2>
        <p>
            This is my engineering notebook. I write about projects while I'm still working on them: what I tried, what
            broke, and what I figured out along the way. It's not a portfolio, so expect unfinished prototypes, dead
            ends, and investigations that don't have an ending yet. I explain why in <a href='/projects/notebook-init/'
                >my first post</a
            >.
        </p>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
            My code is on <a href={GITHUB_URL} target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>GitHub</a>, and you can reach
            me at <EmailLink />. If you're hiring, here's <a href='/benji-tusk-cv.pdf' download>my CV</a> (PDF). When I'm
            not at a computer, I'm usually rollerblading, reading, or out for a walk.
        </p>
    </Prose>
</BaseLayout>
